WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
Start with the product rule.

2
00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:09.120
d by d x of u v equals u d
v by d x, plus v d u by d x.

3
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:13.970
Integrate both sides and rearrange:
a rule for integrating products.

4
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:19.540
Now three integrals: x e to the
x, x times the natural log of x,

5
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:21.950
and x e to the x squared.

6
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.790
All three are products.

7
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.230
Does the new rule help with
every one, or only some?

8
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.320
In this mission, you'll see integration
by parts come straight from the product

9
00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:32.170
rule.

10
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.270
You'll choose which factor
is u, to differentiate,

11
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.400
and which is d v by d x, to integrate.

12
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:42.430
And you'll meet substitution,
the chain rule in reverse.

13
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:46.920
Your mission: decide when the backwards
product rule helps you integrate.
